WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.087 --> 00:00:13.889
brought several changes and surprises to Aunt Polly's house.

2
00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:18.572
One day, as Pollyanna was walking down the road, she found a kitten.

3
00:00:25.898 --> 00:00:28.280
She went door to door, trying to find the kitten's owner.

4
00:00:30.648 --> 00:00:34.451
When no one claimed it, she brought it home to Aunt Polly, who was reading in the sitting

5
00:00:34.491 --> 00:00:42.458
room. "I was glad I didn't find the owner because I wanted to keep it," Pollyanna confessed.

6
00:00:43.779 --> 00:00:48.422
Aunt Polly stared in horror at the neglected animal Pollyanna was cradling in her arms.

7
00:00:50.964 --> 00:00:54.327
She wasn't fond of cats, not even clean, healthy ones.

8
00:00:55.508 --> 00:00:57.049
"What a dirty beast!

9
00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:00.192
I'm sure it's sick and covered with fleas."

10
00:01:02.252 --> 00:01:05.013
"I know."

11
00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:08.334
Pollyanna looked tenderly down at the kitten.

12
00:01:08.354 --> 00:01:12.095
"The poor thing doesn't understand we're going to keep it."

13
00:01:12.115 --> 00:01:16.776
"What?" Aunt Polly dropped her book, startling the kitten.

14
00:01:16.796 --> 00:01:21.638
"I told everybody you'd let me keep it if I couldn't find its owner.

15
00:01:22.098 --> 00:01:23.678
Poor, lonely little thing."

16
00:01:26.079 --> 00:01:30.440
Aunt Polly tried to speak, but once again she had that strange helpless feeling.

17
00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:37.624
"You took me in, so I knew you wouldn't let this kitty hunt for a home," Pollyanna said.

18
00:01:37.644 --> 00:01:43.309
"At least I had the Ladies' Aid out West, but the poor kitty has no one."

19
00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:47.052
Pollyanna ran happily from the room.

20
00:01:47.592 --> 00:01:49.514
"Pollyanna! Pollyanna!

21
00:01:49.874 --> 00:01:54.037
I never said—" But Pollyanna was already halfway to the kitchen.

22
00:01:54.057 --> 00:01:59.722
"Nancy! Come see this sweet kitty that Aunt Polly's letting me keep!

23
00:02:00.142 --> 00:02:01.544
I'm naming her Fluffy!"

24
00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:07.943
Aunt Polly gasped with dismay, but she felt powerless to object.

25
00:02:09.665 --> 00:02:14.749
The next day Pollyanna brought home a dog, even dirtier and more forlorn than the kitten.

26
00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:21.254
Once again Aunt Polly—who disliked dogs even more than cats—said nothing.

27
00:02:22.635 --> 00:02:26.258
How could she protest when Pollyanna saw her as an angel of mercy?

28
00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.984
A few days later, Pollyanna found yet another creature for Aunt Polly to take in.

29
00:02:34.144 --> 00:02:39.188
That morning Aunt Polly gave Pollyanna a break from sewing, so Pollyanna visited Mrs.

30
00:02:39.228 --> 00:02:45.854
Snow. The two had become good friends and often played the Glad Game together.

31
00:02:49.277 --> 00:02:53.660
On the way home, Pollyanna spotted a boy sitting by the road, whittling a stick.

32
00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:57.783
"Hello!" Pollyanna said cheerfully.

33
00:02:59.365 --> 00:03:01.186
The boy glanced up but quickly looked away.

34
00:03:01.206 --> 00:03:03.108
"Hello yourself."

35
00:03:05.024 --> 00:03:08.865
Although Pollyanna liked adults, she really wanted a friend her own age.

36
00:03:10.025 --> 00:03:12.846
So she was determined to make the most of this opportunity.

37
00:03:12.866 --> 00:03:15.967
"My name's Pollyanna Whittier."

38
00:03:17.368 --> 00:03:19.208
She plopped onto the grass near the boy.

39
00:03:19.228 --> 00:03:20.748
"What's yours?"

40
00:03:20.768 --> 00:03:23.149
"Jimmy Bean."

41
00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:25.190
"Where do you live?"

42
00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:29.751
"Nowhere." Pollyanna persisted.

43
00:03:29.771 --> 00:03:32.752
"Everybody lives somewhere."

44
00:03:34.912 --> 00:03:36.273
"I'm hunting for a new place."

45
00:03:36.293 --> 00:03:40.497
"Oh! Where is it?"

46
00:03:40.517 --> 00:03:45.140
"If I knew where it was, I wouldn't be hunting for it."

47
00:03:46.742 --> 00:03:48.363
Jimmy's voice dripped with scorn.

48
00:03:49.624 --> 00:03:54.408
This was not a nice boy, but he was a young person, so Pollyanna tried again.

49
00:03:54.428 --> 00:03:56.930
"Where did you live before?"

50
00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:57.911
she asked.

51
00:03:58.992 --> 00:04:00.613
Jimmy shook his head in disbelief.

52
00:04:01.714 --> 00:04:03.916
"Do you always ask so many questions?"

53
00:04:05.896 --> 00:04:09.198
"If you'd talk more, I wouldn't have to pester you with questions."

54
00:04:11.499 --> 00:04:14.361
"Okay!" Jimmy smiled slightly.

55
00:04:14.381 --> 00:04:20.264
"I'm ten, almost eleven, and I went to live at the Orphans' Home last year.

56
00:04:21.244 --> 00:04:24.166
It's so crowded that I left this morning to find a real home.

57
00:04:24.886 --> 00:04:31.530
If you have a home, you have a family, and I haven't had one since—" Jimmy sniffed as

58
00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:33.031
if trying to hold back tears.

59
00:04:34.412 --> 00:04:36.465
"Since Dad died.

60
00:04:37.325 --> 00:04:41.708
I tried four houses, but nobody wanted me, even though I volunteered to work.

61
00:04:43.009 --> 00:04:44.570
Is that enough information for you?"

62
00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:49.232
"I know just how you feel," Pollyanna said.

63
00:04:49.252 --> 00:04:56.076
"After my father died, there was nobody to take me in until Aunt Polly—" She stopped and her

64
00:04:56.137 --> 00:04:57.898
face lit up.

65
00:04:58.538 --> 00:05:01.600
"Oh! Aunt Polly will be glad to give you a home!

66
00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:07.984
Besides me, she's taken in Fluffy and Buffy, and they're only a cat and a dog."

67
00:05:09.926 --> 00:05:11.087
Jimmy's face brightened.

68
00:05:11.107 --> 00:05:13.209
"Would she really?"

69
00:05:15.771 --> 00:05:19.594
"She's so good and kind, the nicest lady in the world!"

70
00:05:20.735 --> 00:05:22.937
Pollyanna jumped up and started running home.

71
00:05:22.957 --> 00:05:30.604
"There's tons of space in her house, though you may have to start out in the attic room.

72
00:05:31.788 --> 00:05:34.169
But it's even nicer now with window screens."

73
00:05:38.991 --> 00:05:40.712
Jimmy laughed as they ran together.

74
00:05:40.732 --> 00:05:43.954
"I never met anyone who talked so much!"

75
00:05:43.974 --> 00:05:48.096
"You should be glad I do," Pollyanna said.

76
00:05:48.116 --> 00:05:51.377
"Because when I'm talking, you don't have to!"
